# SQL migration files must stay byte-for-byte stable: sqlx verifies a checksum
# of each migration against what was recorded when it was first applied, and an
# EOL conversion (LF<->CRLF) changes the bytes, which makes the app panic on
# startup with "migration N was previously applied but has been modified".
# Freeze them so git never converts line endings.
next/src-tauri/migrations/*.sql -text
